      "excerpt": "Editorial coordination — A retained asynchronous record producer and a caller that selects the first match. Producer cleanup can suspend; the producer is retained independently of the consumer. Predicate may fail and a read may be cancelled."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 1,
      "excerpt": "first_match owns a supplied retained asynchronous record source and a supplied predicate. The source has next/aclose asynchronous operations; cancellation interrupts a suspended read, and cleanup may suspend. Framework ports use actual JS async generators; Python uses actual async for/Task.cancel. Native cursor ports use actual Java CompletionStage, PHP Closure, Ruby blocks or Go typed completion callbacks plus a native completion channel, with native predicate failures. These cursor interfaces are declared adaptations of the original resource carrier, not built-in async-generator claims."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/src/search.js",
      "line": 1,
      "excerpt": "export async function first_match(records,predicate){"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/src/search.js",
      "line": 3,
      "excerpt": "while(true){const row=await records.next();if(row.done)return null;if(predicate(row.value)){return row.value;}}"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/src/search.js",
      "line": 5,
      "excerpt": "}"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/src/Workspace.jsx",
